dho:t-sn46.37 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.37 Āvaraṇanīvaraṇasutta — Obstacles"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Both lists, as citations on the existing lists (1.1, 1.3-1.7; 2.1, 2.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "What the sutta says about them: the hindrances are obstacles and corruptions of the heart that weaken wisdom; the awakening factors are not, and when developed lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom (1.1, 1.8, 2.1, 2.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality does or leads to." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.53 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.53 Aggisutta — Fire"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The timing advice: which awakening factors it is the right or wrong time to develop when the mind is sluggish (4.1, 7.1) or restless (10.1, 13.1), the reason given for each, and 'mindfulness is always useful' (15.4)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The setting and the challenge from wanderers of other religions (1.1-3.1); the four fire similes (5, 8, 11, 14) that illustrate the advice; the repeated statements after each simile (6, 9, 12, 15.1-15.3)." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

